{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>This is what He spoke, etc.</b> Where did He speak? ״וְנֹעַדְתִּי שָׁמָּה לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְנִקְדַּשׁ בִּכְבֹדִי״ (Exodus 29) — do not read בִּכְבֹדִי but rather בִּמְכֻבָּדַי. Moses said to Aaron: Aaron my brother, I knew that the House would be sanctified by the intimates of the Omnipresent, and I supposed it would be either through me or through you. Now I see that they are greater than me and you (Sifra)." "<b>And Aaron was silent.</b> He received reward for his silence. And what reward did he receive? That the Speech was addressed exclusively to him — the section of wine-drinking was stated to him alone (Vayikra Rabbah 12)." "<b>Among those near to Me.</b> Among My chosen ones." "<b>And before all the people I will be glorified.</b> When the Holy One, blessed be He, executes judgment upon the righteous, He is feared and exalted and praised — if so regarding these, all the more so regarding the wicked. And so it says: ״נוֹרָא אֱלֹהִים מִמִּקְדָּשֶׁיךָ״ (Psalms 68) — do not read מִמִּקְדָּשֶׁיךָ but rather מִמְּקֻדָּשֶׁיךָ."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:40.128737005Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}